{"id":13326,"artist":"(Beverly Hill Billies Theme)","title":"BALLAD OF JED CLAMPETT","lyrics_plain":"Come 'n listen to my story\n'Bout a man named Jed\nPoor Mountaineer barely\nKept his family fed\nAn' then one day,\nHe was shootin' at some food,\nAn' up thru the ground\nCame a bubblin' crude.\nOil that is!\nBlack gold!\nTexas tea!\nWell, the first thing ya know,\nJed's a millionaire\nKinfolk said,\n\"Jed, move away from there.\"\nSaid: Californy is\nThe place y'oughta be,\nSo they loaded up the truck,\nAnd they moved to Beverly.\nHills that is!\nSwimmin' pools,\nMovie stars!\nOl' Jed bought a mansion.\nLawdy it was swank\nNext door neighbor was\nPres'dent of the bank,\nLotsa folks objected,\nBut the banker found no fault,\n'Cause ol' Jed's millions\nWas alayin' in the vault\nCash, that is!\nCap'tal gains,\nDepletion money!\nWell now it's time\nTo say goodbye\nTo Jed and all his kin\nAn' they would like to thank\nYou folks fer kindly droppin' in.\nYou're all invited back again\nTo this locality,\nT'have a heapin' helpin'\nOf their hospitality.\nHillbilly, that is!  Set a spell,\nTake your shoes off!\nY'all come back, here!","lyrics_synced":"[00:01.78] Come 'n listen to my story\n[00:03.56] 'Bout a man named Jed\n[00:05.11] Poor Mountaineer barely\n[00:06.56] Kept his family fed\n[00:08.67] An' then one day,\n[00:09.56] He was shootin' at some food,\n[00:12.22] An' up thru the ground\n[00:13.78] Came a bubblin' crude.\n[00:15.56] Oil that is!\n[00:16.44] Black gold!\n[00:17.33] Texas tea!\n[00:18.67] Well, the first thing ya know,\n[00:20.44] Jed's a millionaire\n[00:22.00] Kinfolk said,\n[00:23.11] \"Jed, move away from there.\"\n[00:25.56] Said: Californy is\n[00:26.67] The place y'oughta be,\n[00:29.11] So they loaded up the truck,\n[00:30.67] And they moved to Beverly.\n[00:32.44] Hills that is!\n[00:33.33] Swimmin' pools,\n[00:34.22] Movie stars!\n[00:35.11] Ol' Jed bought a mansion.\n[00:37.33] Lawdy it was swank\n[00:38.89] Next door neighbor was\n[00:40.44] P